  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "description": "Explains what this dashboard or section shows.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Answers:** what the traces can show about the five operator-burden evaluation primitives, and whether an alignment-floor drift event was recorded.\n\n**Data comes from:** primitive 1 needs workflows with human gates; primitive 2 needs tool steps that fail in the sandbox; primitive 4 needs calls to the `anthropic` provider with prompt caching. Primitives 3 and 5 are judged on a holdout set and are not in traces at all. In this version no normal run writes an evaluation score span or a drift event, so those panels show \"No data\" until an evaluation job emits them.\n\nThe stack keeps traces for 24 hours, so no panel can look further back than that."
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Primitive 1 · expected_hitl_invocations_per_session",
      "description": "What do the primitive 1 panels show?",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Counts answered human gates (`hitl.invocation.responded`). Divide by the number of workflow runs to get the per-session figure; the declared roll-up dimensions `agent_role` and `workload_class` are not on these spans, so no panel splits by them."
      },
      "id": 2,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      }
    },
