    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Primitive 3 · sandbox_tier_routing_accuracy",
      "description": "Why is there no panel for primitive 3?",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Not derivable from spans.** This primitive is a holdout judgement (`HOLDOUT_META_JUDGE_RATIO`): a reviewer or judge decides whether each tool call ran at the right sandbox tier. No span carries that verdict. Use `arhugula eval status` to run the holdout assertions and see the result."
      },
      "id": 10,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Primitive 5 · routing_accuracy_holdout",
      "description": "Why is there no panel for primitive 5?",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Not derivable from spans.** This primitive is a holdout judgement (`HOLDOUT_META_JUDGE_RATIO`): a reviewer or judge decides whether each call was routed to the right model. No span carries that verdict. Use `arhugula eval status` to run the holdout assertions and see the result."
      },
      "id": 11,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 24,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Primitive 4 · cache_hit_rate_alignment_floor",
      "description": "What do the primitive 4 panels show?",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Formula: `anthropic.cache_read_input_tokens / (anthropic.cache_read_input_tokens + anthropic.cache_creation_input_tokens)`. TraceQL cannot divide two sums, so the two inputs are shown side by side; divide the first by the sum of both. Only calls to the `anthropic` provider write these attributes. `arhugula eval drift show` reports the computed rate against your threshold."
      },
      "id": 12,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      }
    },
