    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Evaluation score spans and drift events",
      "description": "Why can the score and drift panels be empty?",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "An evaluation job can write one `eval <primitive>` span per score and one `gen_ai.eval.alignment_floor.drift_detected` span event when a value falls below the operator's threshold. No normal workflow run writes either, so these panels stay empty unless such a job runs. `arhugula eval drift show` is the supported way to see drift results; `arhugula eval status` covers the holdout loop."
      },
      "id": 17,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      }
    },
